 "pdf": "ads7067.pdf",
 "pages": "p.3 (RTE pins), p.4 (YBH balls, Table 4-2), p.5 (ROC: DVDD 1.65-5.5 V, AVDD 3-5.5 V; abs max digital inputs 5.5 V), p.8 (tCONV 950 ns, tDEN_CSDO 22 ns, tDZ_CSDO 50 ns, tD_CKDO 16 ns), p.9 (Figures 5-1, 5-2), p.16 (straight binary, Table 6-1), p.20-21 (Figure 6-4, Table 6-4 frames), p.21-22 (Table 6-5 SPI-00 at power-up), p.22 (daisy chain), p.23-24 (Table 6-6 opcodes, Figures 6-9, 6-10), p.25-27 (Table 6-7 modes, Figure 6-13, Table 6-8 on-the-fly), p.28-35 (Table 6-9 registers)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs, internal 2.5 V reference (REF_EN) and the 2 x VREF range (RANGE): every conversion returns the 0 V code 0000h",
  "the SPI mode is fixed at SPI-00 (the power-up protocol); CPOL_CPHA writes are stored only",
  "only the 24-bit frame {result[15:0], 8'b0} is output: the 20-bit averaged result (OSR_CFG), appended channel ID / status flags (APPEND_STATUS), FIX_PAT, CRC (CRC_EN, 32-bit frames, CRCERR_IN) and the diagnostic bit-walk / fixed-voltage test modes do not change it",
  "daisy-chain pass-through of SDI to SDO with a 24-SCLK delay",
  "set bit (18h) is a plain write and clear bit (20h) is ignored (no read-modify-write); RST reads back as written (datasheet: write-only); DIAGNOSTICS_KEY = 96h unlock for C0h-C2h is not checked",
  "manual-mode channel latency: a MANUAL_CHID write at CS rising selects the channel of the conversion started at that edge (the datasheet samples it one cycle later); the on-the-fly 1cccc channel select is accepted in every SEQ_MODE",
  "auto-sequence channel stepping (AUTO_SEQ_CH_SEL, SEQ_START, SEQ_STATUS) and averaging-mode internal conversion starts (OSC_SEL, CLK_DIV, Table 6-3)",
  "GPIOs: PIN_CFG / GPIO_CFG / GPO_OUTPUT_VALUE stored only; AINx/GPIOx pins never driven, GPI_VALUE reads 0",
  "offset calibration (CAL stays as written), BOR on brown-out, 5 ms power-up / reset times, throughput and SCLK limits"
 ],
